          "answer_text": "Throughout almost the entire country, Madagascar's contemporary cuisine typically consists of a base of rice ( vary) served with an accompaniment ( laoka).\n\nMalagasy cuisine reflects the diverse influences of Southeast Asian, African, Oceania, Indian, Chinese, and European culinary traditions.\n\nSoutheast Asian cultural influence is also evident in Malagasy cuisine, in which rice is consumed at every meal, typically accompanied by one of a variety of flavorful vegetable or meat dishes.",
